# Plain-English text for "Needs you" and "Quick" questions.
# NEED[id] = dict(q, why, opts=[(key,label)] or None, rec=key|'y'|None, diag=name|None)
DRAFT_OPTS=[('A','One page with a switch between the two looks'),('B','Keep only the newer page')]
NEED={
# ---- LAG
'LAG-Q2':dict(q='Keep the Home 3D player loaded the whole time you are in menus?',why='Going back to Home takes 4–14 s here, because the player is built again each time. Keeping it uses about 10–20 MB of the phone\'s graphics memory. Medium risk; it gets its own playtest.',rec='y'),
'LAG-Q4':dict(q='After GET OUT THERE, you wait while the commentary plays up to your minute. How should it go?',why='18.5 s of waiting, and only 0.2 s of it is real work. This changes how a match feels.',opts=[('A','As now (18.5 s)'),('B','3× faster (about 6 s)'),('C','Jump straight to your chance')],rec='B',diag='commentary'),
'LAG-Q5':dict(q='The Home player\'s idle animation runs at 30 frames a second. Lower it?',why='Home sitting still keeps the processor busy here: about 1 s of blocking every 5 s. Lower means smoother menus and a slightly less smooth idle.',opts=[('A','Keep 30'),('B','20 a second'),('C','Pause when nothing moves')],rec='B'),
'LAG-Q8':dict(q='On iPhone in Safari, drop the full-screen look completely and show only the "How?" tip?',why='Safari cannot really go full screen. Today a saved "on" turns it on with no way to turn it off. Seen in an iPhone test profile, not real Safari.',rec='y',diag='fullscreen'),
'LAG-Q13':dict(q='How should the first five lag fixes go live?',why='Fixes 1–5 are small and low risk: full screen, the Home photo, the first 3D switch, loading order and graphics checks.',opts=[('A','All five together, then re-measure, then the rest'),('B','One deploy per fix')],rec='A'),
'LAG-Q14':dict(q='You test the lag fixes on your iPhone, plus one Android phone if anyone has one?',why='This computer has no graphics chip, so phone speeds cannot be measured here. Someone has to try it on a real phone.',rec='y'),
'LAG-QB1':dict(q='Old patch-notes pages and playtest notes take 158 MB in the code store. What do we do with them?',why='125 MB of patch notes and 33 MB of playtest notes. Every new chat downloads them. The patch-notes plan wants to add more pages (its "copy pages back" question below).',opts=[('A','Move them out; keep a list of links'),('B','Keep them in a separate big-file store'),('C','Leave them as they are')],rec='A'),
'LAG-QB9':dict(q='There are two Draft test pages that differ by one screen. Which do we keep?',why='The two plans disagree. The lag plan says keep only the newer page. The admin plan says one page with a switch. Pick the same answer in both places.',opts=DRAFT_OPTS,rec='B'),
'LAG-QB10':dict(q='Mikey\'s copy of the match engine: move the parts he wants into the real game, then delete the copy?',why='418 KB of copied engine, still on the build guard\'s list of copies. It is Mikey\'s page, and the admin plan says keep it until he decides.',rec='y'),
'LAG-QB11':dict(q='Delete the "Bigger players" and "Zoom-to-play" test pages, and add Tournaments to the admin menu?',why='None of the three is in the menu or linked. Their looks were decided on 12 Oct. The admin plan instead keeps the first two as old tests.',rec='y'),
'LAG-QB12':dict(q='Ten one-off test pages: each owner says keep or delete?',why='Bicycle kick, spin, dribble, attack, tuning, sound, the old 3D page, American draft, new profile and draft preview. Last changed 26 Sep – 5 Oct. No visit records, so only their owners know. Needs Mikey and Leo.',rec='y'),
'LAG-QB13':dict(q='Delete the separate Scenario Builder page? The same tool is a tab in the gallery.',why='The admin plan instead keeps it in Old tests. You lose nothing either way.',rec='y'),
'LAG-QB14':dict(q='Ask Mikey whether manager mode is still a live game?',why='It is in no guide and no link, and was last changed on 2 Sep. His answer decides whether it gets cleaned up.',rec='y'),
'LAG-QB25':dict(q='Start with trimming the notes file every chat reads, before the lag fixes?',why='The cheapest win: about 88k tokens saved on every turn of every chat. Then lag fixes 1–5. Deletions come last.',rec='y'),
# ---- TB
'TB-Q1':dict(q='How should progress bars reach the team board?',why='Claude has forgotten to send updates twice. Automatic costs no tokens. A command costs about 50k tokens a day per person.',opts=[('A','Automatic, at the end of each turn'),('B','Claude sends them by hand')],rec='A'),
'TB-Q6':dict(q='Set the team board up for cloud chats only, for now?',why='A chat on someone\'s own computer only sends updates if its copy of the code is current, and pulling does not work for you. Ask Leo and Mikey if they use Claude on their own computer.',rec='y'),
# ---- ADM
'ADM-Q1':dict(q='Keep testers out of the 26 pages that change shared data, sit in the admin area, or show real-match data we have no licence to share?',why='Testers can open 52 pages today. This makes it 43. They lose pages like Club Data and the XP book.',rec='y'),
'ADM-Q3':dict(q='Mark you as owner of the old site and Draft test pages, and ask Mikey and Leo about Tuning, First-person dribble and Live attack?',why='The history in this copy starts on 3 Sep, so these owners cannot be proven. The owner decides each page\'s future.',rec='y'),
'ADM-Q42':dict(q='Keep the Champions League Draft admin page, once its owner confirms?',why='Its owner is not proven. The other choice is to move it to Old tests.',rec='y'),
'ADM-Q68':dict(q='There are two Draft test pages that differ by one screen. Which do we keep?',why='Same choice as in the lag plan, which recommends the other answer. Pick the same answer in both places.',opts=DRAFT_OPTS,rec='A'),
'ADM-Q84':dict(q='Keep Mikey\'s match engine copy until Mikey decides to retire it?',why='The lag plan wants it moved into the game and deleted. It is the same decision, and it is Mikey\'s call.',rec='y'),
'ADM-Q110':dict(q='If a new admin page is missing from the page list, should that block the deploy?',why='Like the one-engine guard: it stops a deploy until the list is fixed, for all three of you. The other choice only fails when tests are run.',opts=[('A','Block the deploy'),('B','Fail only in the test run')],rec='A'),
'ADM-Q146':dict(q='Before building, you go through the list of 70 admin pages (name, home, keep or old, owner)?',why='Every name and place on the new admin home comes straight from that list. It is about 70 rows to check.',rec='y'),
'ADM-Q151':dict(q='Do a Higgsfield design pass for the new admin home before it is built?',why='Your rule: plan, design, then build. It costs Higgsfield credits and one round of looking at pictures.',rec='y'),
# ---- PN
'PN-Q3':dict(q='Leo\'s second "v0.16" becomes Leo v0.17?',why='Two of Leo\'s notes are both called v0.16 (13 and 14 Oct). Needs Leo\'s yes.',rec='y'),
'PN-Q7':dict(q='If two patch notes get the same number, should that block the deploy?',why='15 number clashes have happened so far. Blocking stops a deploy until the clash is fixed, for all three of you.',opts=[('A','Block the deploy'),('B','Warn only')],rec='A'),
'PN-Q9':dict(q='Copy the missing patch-notes pages back from claude.ai into the code, pictures only (no videos)?',why='12 pages exist only on claude.ai. This adds to the 125 MB the lag plan wants to move out. Answer it together with that big-files question.',rec='y'),
'PN-Q40':dict(q='Will you look in claude.ai\'s version history for your lost v0.51 page?',why='Its link now shows v0.52, and only you can see older versions. Optional: if not, v0.51 is kept as text only.',rec=None),
'PN-Q57':dict(q='Will you check your claude.ai list once, for patch notes no file mentions?',why='I can only find links written in the code: 69 so far. Any others would be missed.',rec='y'),
'PN-Q197':dict(q='You send Leo and Mikey one message each, asking them to agree to the new numbering?',why='Each person counts only their own notes from now on, and Leo\'s note becomes v0.17. It changes every future patch note they write.',rec='y'),
}

